# Architecture — SOLID, KISS, DRY, YAGNI

## YAGNI

- **You Aren't Gonna Need It** — the best code is the code you don't write.
- Don't implement features that aren't requested. Avoid speculative abstractions and «nice to have» additions until there's a real requirement.
- When in doubt — leave it out.

## SOLID

- **S (Single Responsibility)** — one class/module = one area of responsibility. Split large services into smaller ones.
- **O (Open/Closed)** — open for extension, closed for modification. Prefer composition and dependency injection over changing existing code.
- **L (Liskov Substitution)** — subtypes must be replaceable by the base type without breaking behavior.
- **I (Interface Segregation)** — narrow interfaces over «fat» ones. Don't force clients to depend on methods they don't use.
- **D (Dependency Inversion)** — depend on abstractions (interfaces), not on concrete implementations. In NestJS — inject services via constructor.

## KISS

- Prefer the simplest solution first. Don't over-engineer.
- Avoid unnecessary abstractions, patterns, and layers until there is a real need.

## DRY

- Don't duplicate logic. Extract repeated code into functions, helpers, or shared services.
- When duplication appears — assess whether an abstraction (shared module, common service) is needed or a single call site suffices.

## Examples

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — SRP violation: сервис и парсинг в одном месте
class ProductService {
  parseOzonResponse(raw: string) { /* ... */ }
  parseWbResponse(raw: string) { /* ... */ }
  createProduct() { /* ... */ }
}

// ✅ GOOD — разделение ответственностей
class OzonParser { parse(raw: string) { /* ... */ } }
class WbParser { parse(raw: string) { /* ... */ } }
class ProductService { /* product business logic only */ }
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — DRY violation
if (platform === 'ozon') {
  const url = `https://api.ozon.ru/v1/product/${id}`;
  const res = await fetch(url, { headers: { ... } });
  return res.json();
}
if (platform === 'wb') {
  const url = `https://suppliers-api.wildberries.ru/api/v1/product/${id}`;
  const res = await fetch(url, { headers: { ... } });
  return res.json();
}

// ✅ GOOD — common approach, details in implementation
const client = marketClients.get(platform);
return client.getProduct(id);
```
